  "how_introduced": "This commit rewrote installation to a standalone installer and reimplemented the `prek-version` handling in a still-vulnerable way. It introduced `VERSION=\"${{ inputs.prek-version }}\"` inside bash and an unquoted `curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf ${{ steps.resolve.outputs.base_url }}prek-installer.sh | sh`, both of which are exactly the lines the fix changes to env-based/quoted forms. Even though an earlier commit had already introduced `prek-version` unsafely, this commit is a vulnerable reimplementation and therefore also a bug-introducing commit.",
