            "model": "gpt-5.4",
            "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
            "reasoning": "This commit did not originate the `extra_args` sink from the screening hypothesis, but it did introduce a separate injection sink that the fix later hardens. It added the `prek-version` input and inlined `${{ inputs.prek-version }}` directly into a bash `if` test and a `python -m pip install prek==...` command, which is the exact unsafe composite-action pattern the fix replaces with env-based handling. `git log -S` for `${{ inputs.prek-version }}` and the affected strings points back to this commit as the first introduction of that vulnerable pattern.",
